-----------------------------------\par
\par
CALCULATION OF NO. OF PILES\par
---------------------------\par
\par
\par
Total Vertical load at cg of pile cap = tvl = 1042.508 t \par
Total Horizontal force = thf = 34.730 t\par
Seismic Horizontal force = shf = 140.800 t \par
Vertical Load Capacity of pile = vc = 250.000 t\par
\par
Horizontal Load Capacity of Pile = hc = 20.000 t \par
\par
No. of Plies required (Vertical) = vpn = tvl / vc = 1042.508 / 250.000 = 4.170 nos \par
\par
No. of Plies required (Horizontal) = hpn = tvl / vc = 34.730 / 20.000 = 1.736 nos \par
\par
No. of Plies required (Horizontal- in Seismic Case) = shf / (hc*1.25)\par
                                                    = 140.800 / (20.000*1.25)\par
                                                    = 5.632 nos \par
\par
Provided No of piles = 6 nos \par
\par
\par
STRUCTURAL DESIGN OF PILE\par
-------------------------\par
\par
\par
Maximum Lateral Force in Longitudinal Direction on Pile Foundation under normal condition = mlfl = 34.730 t\par
\par
Corresponding Max. Vertical Load on one Pile for Load - Normal Case = cmaxvl1 = 505.800 t\par
and Corresponding Minimum Vertical Load on one Pile for Load - Normal Case = cminvl1 = -158.297 t\par
\par
Maximum Lateral Force in Longitudinal Direction on Pile Foundation under Seismic Condition = 140.800 t\par
\par
Corresponding Maximum Vertical Load on one Pile - Seismic case = 1083.242 t \par
Corresponding Minimum Vertical Load on one Pile - Seismic case = -667.699 t \par
\par
Total No. of Piles = tp = 6\par
Length of Pile = lp = 20 m \par
Diameter of Pile = dp = 1.2 m \par
\par
LOAD CALCULATIONS FOR STRUCTURAL DESIGN \par
----------------------------------------\par
\par
\par
a) Normal Case \par
--------------\par
Max. Lateral Force on one Pile under Normal Condition = Q = 34.730 / 6.000 = 5.788 t  = 6 t\par
\par
Max. Lateral load Capacity of Pile under Normal Condition = 20.000  t  > 6.000 t, SO,   OK\par
Now, Maximum Moment in Pile is given by = 2.95*Q tm \par
Therefore, Maximum Moment in Pile under Normal condition = mmp = 2.95*6 = 17.700 t-m \par
\par
Corresponding Maximum Vertical Load (Excluding Self Weight of pile) = 505.800 t \par
\par
Corresponding Minimum Vertical Load (Excluding Self Weight of pile) = -158.297 t \par
\par
\par
b) Seismic Case \par
----------------\par
\par
Maximum Lateral Force on one Pile under Seismic Condition = shf/tp = 140.800 / 6 = 23.467 t \par
\par
Max. Lateral load Capacity of Pile under Seismic Condition = 1.25 x hc\par
                                                           = 1.25 x 20.000\par
                                                           = 25.000 t > 23.467, SO   OK.\par
\par
\par
Maximum Moment in Pile under Seismic condition = 2.95*Q = 2.95*23.467 = 69.226 tm \par
\par
Corresponding Maximum Vertical Load (Excluding Self Weight of pile) = 1083.242 t \par
Corresponding Minimum Vertical Load (Excluding Self Weight of pile) = -667.699 t  \par
\par
Self weight of pile = pwt = conc_den * Pile_len * \f1\'f0 * pcdia^2 / 4  = 54.3 t \par
                          = 2.400 * 20.000 * 3.14159 * 1.200^2 / 4\par
                          = 54.287 t \par
\par
The design loads and moments are summarised below : \par
\par
Sr. No. Description                  Vertical Load (t)     Moment (tm)   Eccentricity M/V (m) \par
\par
1. Normal Case (Max. Vertical load)         505.800            17.700              0.035\par
2. Normal Case (Min. Vertical Load)        -158.297            17.700             -0.112\par
3. Seismic Case (Max. Vertical Load)       1083.242            69.226              0.064\par
4. Seismic Case (Min. Vertical Load)       -667.699            69.226             -0.104\par
\par
Calculation of Reinforcement\par
-----------------------------\par
\par
The reinforcement in pile assumed 0.83% of cross-sectional area. 0.83% of c/s area \par
\par
Area of Reinforcement = ar_rein = (rpa / 100) * \'f0 * (pcdia * 100)^2\par
                                = (0.830 / 100) * 3.142 * (1.200 * 100)^2\par
                                = 93.871 Sq.cm \par
\par
\par
Bar dia to be provided = bdia = 25 mm \par
No. of 25 dia. Bars reqd. = ar_rein / (\'f0 * bdia^2 / 400.0) = 19 No. \par
                           = 93.871 / (3.14159 * 25.000^2 / 400.0)\par
                           = 19.123 \par
                           = 19.000 Nos\par
\par
\par
No. of 25 dia. Bars prov. = 22 No. \par
\par
\par
Provide 25 dia , 22 nos. around periphery \par
\par
As provided = bar_prvd * (Math.PI * bdia^2 / 400.0)\par
            = 22 * (3.14159 * 25.000^2 / 400.0) \par
            = 107.992 Sq.cm\par
\par
\par
Provide 8 dia. @ 150mm as helical reinforcement \par
\par
